IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc29-xxvii-b-information-trial`

-- ccc29-tests-xxvii-b.l4 -- tests for sections 788 to 809 of the Criminal Code (Canada).
-- Every expected value is written from the text before the run, beside its assertion.
-- The argument order of each function is its GIVEN order in the module.

§ `Tests -- sections 788 to 789`

-- 788(1): proceedings under this Part shall be commenced by laying an information in Form 2.
#ASSERT `s 788(1) the proceedings are required to be commenced by laying an information in Form 2` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 788(1) the proceedings are required to be commenced by laying an information in Form 2` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 788(1) the proceedings are required to be commenced by laying an information in Form 2` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- 788(2): one justice may (a) receive, (b) issue a summons or warrant, (c) do all other things preliminary; an act at or after the trial is not named.
#ASSERT `s 788(2) one justice may do the act` `s 788(2)(a) receive the information` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 788(2) one justice may do the act` `s 788(2)(b) issue a summons or warrant with respect to the information` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 788(2) one justice may do the act` `s 788(2)(c) do all other things preliminary to the trial` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 788(2) one justice may do the act` `s 788(2) an act at or after the trial` EQUALS NOTHING
-- 789(1)(a), (b).
#ASSERT `s 789(1)(a) the information is required to be in writing and under oath` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 789(1)(a) the information is required to be in writing and under oath` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 789(1)(b) the information may charge more than one offence or relate to more than one matter of complaint` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 789(1)(b) the information may charge more than one offence or relate to more than one matter of complaint` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 789(1)(b) each offence or matter of complaint is required to be set out in a separate count` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 789(1)(b) each offence or matter of complaint is required to be set out in a separate count` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 789(1)(b) each offence or matter of complaint is required to be set out in a separate count` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 789(2): no reference to previous convictions where a greater punishment may be imposed by reason of them.
#ASSERT `s 789(2) the information is barred from containing any reference to previous convictions` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 789(2) the information is barred from containing any reference to previous convictions` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- sections 790 to 797`

-- 790(1): a justice who commenced or issued process is not required to be the trial justice.
#ASSERT `s 790(1) the justice is not required to be a justice before whom the trial is held` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 790(1) the justice is not required to be a justice before whom the trial is held` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 790(2): two or more justices act together at the trial; one justice may thereafter do anything.
#ASSERT `s 790(2) the justices are required to be present and act together at the trial` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 790(2) the justices are required to be present and act together at the trial` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 790(2) one justice may do anything required or authorized to be done in connection with the proceedings` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 790(2) one justice may do anything required or authorized to be done in connection with the proceedings` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 790(2) one justice may do anything required or authorized to be done in connection with the proceedings` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 794(1): no need to set out or negative an exception.
#ASSERT `s 794(1) the information need not set out or negative the exception, exemption, proviso, excuse or qualification` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 794(1) the information need not set out or negative the exception, exemption, proviso, excuse or qualification` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 795: Parts XVI and XVIII only for compelling appearance; XVIII.1, XX and XX.1 insofar as not inconsistent; XXII.01 without limit; another Part is not covered.
#ASSERT `s 795 the provisions apply, with any necessary modifications, to proceedings under this Part` `s 795 Part XVI` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 795 the provisions apply, with any necessary modifications, to proceedings under this Part` `s 795 Part XVI` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 795 the provisions apply, with any necessary modifications, to proceedings under this Part` `s 795 Part XVIII` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 795 the provisions apply, with any necessary modifications, to proceedings under this Part` `s 795 Part XVIII.1` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 795 the provisions apply, with any necessary modifications, to proceedings under this Part` `s 795 Part XVIII.1` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 795 the provisions apply, with any necessary modifications, to proceedings under this Part` `s 795 Part XX` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 795 the provisions apply, with any necessary modifications, to proceedings under this Part` `s 795 Part XX` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 795 the provisions apply, with any necessary modifications, to proceedings under this Part` `s 795 Part XX.1` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 795 the provisions apply, with any necessary modifications, to proceedings under this Part` `s 795 Part XX.1` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 795 the provisions apply, with any necessary modifications, to proceedings under this Part` `s 795 Part XXII.01` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 795 the provisions apply, with any necessary modifications, to proceedings under this Part` `s 795 another Part` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- sections 798 to 803`

-- 798: jurisdiction of a summary conviction court.
#ASSERT `s 798 the summary conviction court has jurisdiction to try, determine and adjudge the proceedings` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 798 the summary conviction court has jurisdiction to try, determine and adjudge the proceedings` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 798 the summary conviction court has jurisdiction to try, determine and adjudge the proceedings` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 798 the summary conviction court has jurisdiction to try, determine and adjudge the proceedings` NOTHING TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 799: arguments are (the Part applies, the defendant appears, the prosecutor had due notice, the prosecutor does not appear, the course).
#ASSERT `s 799 the summary conviction court may take the course` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `s 799 dismiss the information` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 799 the summary conviction court may take the course` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `s 799 adjourn the trial to some other time on such terms as it considers proper` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 799 the summary conviction court may take the course` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `s 799 another course` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 799 the summary conviction court may take the course` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE `s 799 dismiss the information` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 799 the summary conviction court may take the course` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE `s 799 dismiss the information` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 799 the summary conviction court may take the course` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `s 799 dismiss the information` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 800(1): both appear.
#ASSERT `s 800(1) the summary conviction court is required to hold the trial` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 800(1) the summary conviction court is required to hold the trial` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 800(2): ways of appearing; require personal appearance; warrant.
#ASSERT `s 800(2) a defendant may appear in the way` `s 800(2) personally` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 800(2) a defendant may appear in the way` `s 800(2) by counsel` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 800(2) a defendant may appear in the way` `s 800(2) by agent` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 800(2) a defendant may appear in the way` `s 800(2) in another way` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 800(2) the summary conviction court may require the defendant to appear personally` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 800(2) the summary conviction court may require the defendant to appear personally` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 800(2) the summary conviction court may issue a warrant in Form 7 for the arrest of the defendant and adjourn the trial to await the defendant's appearance` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 800(2) the summary conviction court may issue a warrant in Form 7 for the arrest of the defendant and adjourn the trial to await the defendant's appearance` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 800(3): an organization appears by counsel or agent; ex parte if it does not appear, on proof of service. The organization question is the s 2 answer (a MAYBE BOOLEAN, an input here).
#ASSERT `s 800(3) the organization is required to appear by counsel or agent` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 800(3) the organization is required to appear by counsel or agent` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 800(3) the organization is required to appear by counsel or agent` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 800(3) the summary conviction court may proceed ex parte to hold the trial` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 800(3) the summary conviction court may proceed ex parte to hold the trial` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 800(3) the summary conviction court may proceed ex parte to hold the trial` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 800(3) the summary conviction court may proceed ex parte to hold the trial` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 800(3) the summary conviction court may proceed ex parte to hold the trial` NOTHING TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 801: arraignment.
#ASSERT `s 801(1) the substance of the information is required to be stated to the defendant` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 801(1) the substance of the information is required to be stated to the defendant` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 801(1)(a) the defendant is required to be asked whether they plead guilty or not guilty to the information` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 801(1)(a) the defendant is required to be asked whether they plead guilty or not guilty to the information` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 801(1)(b) the defendant is required to be asked whether they have cause to show why an order should not be made against them` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 801(1)(b) the defendant is required to be asked whether they have cause to show why an order should not be made against them` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 801(2) the summary conviction court is required to convict the defendant, discharge the defendant under section 730 or make an order against the defendant` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 801(2) the summary conviction court is required to convict the defendant, discharge the defendant under section 730 or make an order against the defendant` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 801(2) the summary conviction court is required to convict the defendant, discharge the defendant under section 730 or make an order against the defendant` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 801(3) the summary conviction court is required to proceed with the trial and take the evidence in accordance with Part XVIII` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 801(3) the summary conviction court is required to proceed with the trial and take the evidence in accordance with Part XVIII` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 801(3) the summary conviction court is required to proceed with the trial and take the evidence in accordance with Part XVIII` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 802.
#ASSERT `s 802(1) the prosecutor is entitled personally to conduct the case` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 802(1) the prosecutor is entitled personally to conduct the case` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 802(1) the defendant is entitled to make full answer and defence` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 802(1) the defendant is entitled to make full answer and defence` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 802(2) the prosecutor or defendant may examine and cross-examine witnesses in the way` `s 802(2) personally` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 802(2) the prosecutor or defendant may examine and cross-examine witnesses in the way` `s 802(2) by counsel` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 802(2) the prosecutor or defendant may examine and cross-examine witnesses in the way` `s 802(2) by agent` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 802(2) the prosecutor or defendant may examine and cross-examine witnesses in the way` `s 802(2) in another way` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 802(3) the witness is required to be examined under oath` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 802(3) the witness is required to be examined under oath` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 802.1: arguments are (the longest term in months, organization (s 2), appearing to request an adjournment, the agent is authorized under a program). More than six months and none of (a), (b), (c): barred.
#ASSERT `s 802.1 the defendant is barred from appearing or examining or cross-examining witnesses by agent` 7 (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 802.1 the defendant is barred from appearing or examining or cross-examining witnesses by agent` 6 (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 802.1 the defendant is barred from appearing or examining or cross-examining witnesses by agent` 24 (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 802.1 the defendant is barred from appearing or examining or cross-examining witnesses by agent` 7 (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 802.1 the defendant is barred from appearing or examining or cross-examining witnesses by agent` 7 (JUST FALSE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 802.1 the defendant is barred from appearing or examining or cross-examining witnesses by agent` 7 NOTHING FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 802.1 the defendant is barred from appearing or examining or cross-examining witnesses by agent` 7 NOTHING TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 803(1): before or during the trial.
#ASSERT `s 803(1) the summary conviction court may adjourn the trial to a time and place to be appointed and stated in the presence of the parties or their counsel or agents` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 803(1) the summary conviction court may adjourn the trial to a time and place to be appointed and stated in the presence of the parties or their counsel or agents` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 803(1.1).
#ASSERT `s 803(1.1) the summary conviction court is required to consider the interests of justice` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 803(1.1) the summary conviction court is required to consider the interests of justice` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 803(1.1) the summary conviction court is required to consider the interests of any victim of the offence in question` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 803(1.1) the summary conviction court is required to consider the interests of any victim of the offence in question` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 803(1.1) the summary conviction court is required to consider the interests of any victim of the offence in question` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 803(2)(a), (b): arguments are (does not appear at the appointed time and place after notice, does not appear for the resumption).
#ASSERT `s 803(2)(a) the summary conviction court may proceed ex parte to hear and determine the proceedings in the absence of the defendant` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 803(2)(a) the summary conviction court may proceed ex parte to hear and determine the proceedings in the absence of the defendant` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 803(2)(a) the summary conviction court may proceed ex parte to hear and determine the proceedings in the absence of the defendant` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 803(2)(b) the summary conviction court may issue a warrant in Form 7 for the arrest of the defendant and adjourn the trial to await their appearance under the warrant` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 803(2)(b) the summary conviction court may issue a warrant in Form 7 for the arrest of the defendant and adjourn the trial to await their appearance under the warrant` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 803(2)(b) the summary conviction court may issue a warrant in Form 7 for the arrest of the defendant and adjourn the trial to await their appearance under the warrant` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 803(3), (4).
#ASSERT `s 803(3) the consent of the Attorney General is required before the proceedings under section 145 are instituted or proceeded with` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 803(3) the consent of the Attorney General is required before the proceedings under section 145 are instituted or proceeded with` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 803(3) the consent of the Attorney General is required before the proceedings under section 145 are instituted or proceeded with` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 803(4) the summary conviction court may dismiss the information with or without costs` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 803(4) the summary conviction court may dismiss the information with or without costs` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests -- sections 804 to 809`

-- 804.
#ASSERT `s 804 the summary conviction court is required to convict the defendant, discharge the defendant under section 730, make an order against the defendant or dismiss the information` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 804 the summary conviction court is required to convict the defendant, discharge the defendant under section 730, make an order against the defendant or dismiss the information` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 806(1): the minute; the conviction or order and certified copy on request; the form to draw up.
#ASSERT `s 806(1) a minute or memorandum indicating that the matter was dealt with under this Part is required to be made by the summary conviction court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 806(1) a minute or memorandum indicating that the matter was dealt with under this Part is required to be made by the summary conviction court` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 806(1) a conviction or order in Form 35 or 36 and a certified copy are required to be drawn up and the certified copy delivered to the person making the request` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 806(1) a conviction or order in Form 35 or 36 and a certified copy are required to be drawn up and the certified copy delivered to the person making the request` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 806(1) the form to be drawn up` TRUE EQUALS `s 806(1) Form 35, a conviction`
#ASSERT `s 806(1) the form to be drawn up` FALSE EQUALS `s 806(1) Form 36, an order`
-- 806(2), (3).
#ASSERT `s 806(2) the summary conviction court is required to issue a warrant of committal in Form 21 or 22` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 806(2) the summary conviction court is required to issue a warrant of committal in Form 21 or 22` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 806(2) section 528 applies in respect of the warrant of committal` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 806(2) section 528 applies in respect of the warrant of committal` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 806(3) the copy of the warrant of committal is admissible in evidence in any proceeding` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 806(3) the copy of the warrant of committal is admissible in evidence in any proceeding` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 806(3) the copy of the warrant of committal is admissible in evidence in any proceeding` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 806(3) the copy of the warrant of committal is admissible in evidence in any proceeding` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 807: arguments of the first function are (several offenders each adjudged to pay, the value of the injury, the costs); of the second, with the total adjudged third. Injury 100, costs 20: the person aggrieved gets at most 120; of 3 x 100 adjudged the residue is 180.
#ASSERT `s 807 the most that is to be paid to the person aggrieved` TRUE 100 20 EQUALS JUST 120
#ASSERT `s 807 the most that is to be paid to the person aggrieved` FALSE 100 20 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 807 the residue to be applied in the manner in which other penalties imposed by law are directed to be applied` TRUE 300 100 20 EQUALS JUST 180
#ASSERT `s 807 the residue to be applied in the manner in which other penalties imposed by law are directed to be applied` TRUE 120 100 20 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 807 the residue to be applied in the manner in which other penalties imposed by law are directed to be applied` TRUE 50 100 20 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 807 the residue to be applied in the manner in which other penalties imposed by law are directed to be applied` FALSE 300 100 20 EQUALS NOTHING
-- 808(1): arguments are (the court dismisses an information, the defendant requests an order of dismissal).
#ASSERT `s 808(1) the summary conviction court may draw up an order of dismissal` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 808(1) the summary conviction court may draw up an order of dismissal` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 808(1) the summary conviction court may draw up an order of dismissal` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 808(1) the summary conviction court is required to give the defendant a certified copy of the order of dismissal` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 808(1) the summary conviction court is required to give the defendant a certified copy of the order of dismissal` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 808(2) the certified copy of the order of dismissal is a bar to the subsequent proceedings` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 808(2) the certified copy of the order of dismissal is a bar to the subsequent proceedings` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 808(2) the certified copy of the order of dismissal is a bar to the subsequent proceedings` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 809(1): arguments are (the court convicts or makes an order [dismisses an information], it considers the costs reasonable and not inconsistent with the section 840 fees).
#ASSERT `s 809(1)(a) the summary conviction court may award costs to be paid to the informant by the defendant` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 809(1)(a) the summary conviction court may award costs to be paid to the informant by the defendant` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 809(1)(a) the summary conviction court may award costs to be paid to the informant by the defendant` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 809(1)(b) the summary conviction court may award costs to be paid to the defendant by the informant` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 809(1)(b) the summary conviction court may award costs to be paid to the defendant by the informant` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 809(1)(b) the summary conviction court may award costs to be paid to the defendant by the informant` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 809(2) the order for costs is required to be set out in the conviction, order or order of dismissal` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 809(2) the order for costs is required to be set out in the conviction, order or order of dismissal` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 809(3): the fine of 500 and costs of 50 are adjudged: the defendant is liable to serve the term for 550.
#ASSERT `s 809(3) the amount for which the defendant is liable to serve the term of imprisonment imposed in default of payment` TRUE 500 50 EQUALS JUST 550
#ASSERT `s 809(3) the amount for which the defendant is liable to serve the term of imprisonment imposed in default of payment` FALSE 500 50 EQUALS NOTHING
-- 809(4): no fine, costs awarded: one month.
#ASSERT `s 809(4) the person who is liable to pay the costs is, in default of payment, liable to imprisonment for one month` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 809(4) the person who is liable to pay the costs is, in default of payment, liable to imprisonment for one month` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 809(4) the person who is liable to pay the costs is, in default of payment, liable to imprisonment for one month` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 809(4) the term of imprisonment in default of payment of the costs`'s `months`) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `s 809(5) costs` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 809(5) costs` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 809(5) costs` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Regulative rules -- sections 788, 800, 804 and 806`

-- These rules cannot be asserted with EQUALS on the stable binary; they are run with #TRACE and read.
-- 788(1): the informant lays the information: the duty is discharged (the trace ends FULFILLED).
#TRACE `s 788(1) the informant is to lay an information in Form 2` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the informant` DOES `s 788 lay an information in Form 2` AT 1
-- 800(1): the court holds the trial.
#TRACE `s 800(1) the court is to hold the trial` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 800 hold the trial` AT 1
-- 804: the court decides to convict, to discharge, to make an order, or to dismiss.
#TRACE `s 804 the court is to decide` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 804 the court decides` `s 804 dismiss the information` AT 1
-- 806(2): the court issues the warrant of committal.
#TRACE `s 806(2) the court is to issue a warrant of committal` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 806 issue a warrant of committal in Form 21 or 22` AT 1
